From: QiuSimons <45143996+QiuSimons@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nat: add BCM expectation-based full-cone NAT support

Add Broadcom expectation-based full-cone NAT support for IPv4 and IPv6.

Full-cone NAT is implemented via a wildcard-source conntrack expectation
keyed on the external mapped address and port. Any incoming packet matching
the external address and port creates a related connection translated to
the internal endpoint.

Key characteristics:
- Endpoint-Independent Mapping (RFC 4787 REQ-1) via nf_nat_src_mapping().
- Port Preservation (RFC 4787 REQ-3) and Parity Preservation (RFC 4787 REQ-4).
- Userspace attaches the BCM-NAT (IPv4) or BCM-NAT6 (IPv6) helper to the
  connection using "ct helper set" prior to masquerade.
- Full compatibility with Netfilter software flowtable offloading (IPS_FULLCONE).
- Clean fallback to symmetric NAT when expectation tables are exhausted.

Signed-off-by: QiuSimons <45143996+QiuSimons@users.noreply.github.com>
---

